{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Symptom\n\nA Gerrit change that has satisfied both merge gates cannot be submitted by the identity the agent workflow is meant to use. Change 2986 sat at `Verified +1`, `LLM-Review +1`, `unresolved_comment_count: 0`, and `submittable: true`, and the revision-scoped submit returned:\n\n```\nHTTP 403\nsubmit not permitted\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe `rebar-review-bot` account is a Gerrit `SERVICE_USER`. Its group memberships are `Registered Users`, `Anonymous Users`, `Service Users`, and its own per-user group. It is **not** a member of `Contributors`, which is one of the groups the `rebar` project's access config references alongside `Administrators` and `feature-branch-drivers`.\n\nGerrit computes permitted actions per caller. Querying the change as the bot returns `actions: ['followup']` with no `submit` entry, while `submittable` is independently `true`. So this is an ACL outcome, not a transient fault and not a gate problem — the change really is ready, and this identity really has no Submit permission.\n\nThe bot's other capabilities are intact: it authenticates (`/a/accounts/self` returns 200), it reads, it votes `LLM-Review`, and it pushes to `refs/for/main` over HTTPS.\n\n## Why this matters\n\n`AGENTS.md` instructs agents to land their own work: \"Land it yourself with revision-scoped Gerrit Submit once both votes are green.\" That instruction is currently not executable by the bot identity. The working arrangement is to submit with the Gerrit administrator credential from SSM instead, which is how change 2986 was landed.\n\nThat arrangement is wrong in three ways:\n\n1. **It escalates routine landings to administrator.** Submitting is a mechanical action gated on two votes the submitter did not cast, so it does not need administrator rights.\n2. **It couples the delivery loop to a human-scoped credential.** Any rotation or scoping change to the administrator credential silently halts all landing.\n3. **The audit trail misattributes every merge.** The submitter recorded on each change is the administrator, not the identity that actually did the work, which defeats the session-hashtag ownership convention the project relies on under a shared bot account.\n\nNote that this is a permission gap, not a gate weakness. The two merge gates are unaffected: the bot cannot vote `Verified`, and it cannot approve its own `LLM-Review`, so granting Submit does not let it self-approve anything.\n\n## Decision (user, 2026-10-25): land through the landing bot; no grant to the review bot\nSupersedes the 2026-09-20 choice to give `rebar-review-bot` Submit. The identity that lands changes is\n`RebarBotNava`, which is in `Contributors` and holds Submit but neither gate label. Giving the review bot\nSubmit as well would put author, both voters and lander in one account, because `Service Users` already\nholds `label-LLM-Review` and `label-Verified`. No Gerrit access change is made.\n\nMeasured 2026-10-25: changes 3109 and 3110 were owned and submitted by `RebarBotNava`; `LLM-Review` came from\n`rebar-review-bot` and `Verified` from `rebar-ci-bot`; no administrator credential was involved.\n\n## Plan\n1. `CONTRIBUTING.md` section 2e: replace \"There is no landing bot, queue, or hand-off label\" with the real\n   division: no queue or hand-off label; Submit is run by a `Contributors` member, on the shared agent setup\n   the landing bot `RebarBotNava`, which cannot vote; the votes come from the review bot and the CI bot.\n2. `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` section 6a: state the same for the `Contributors` bullet.\n3. Leave `AGENTS.md`, `infra/gerrit/` and `scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py` unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `CONTRIBUTING.md` section 2e and `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` section 6a agree: Submit is run by a `Contributors` member (the landing bot `RebarBotNava`), which holds no gate label, and the votes come from the review bot and the CI bot (checked: `grep -n \"no landing bot\" CONTRIBUTING.md` returns nothing; both files name `RebarBotNava` and both vote sources).\n- [ ] The change grants nothing: no diff under `infra/gerrit/`, so label permissions and the two submit requirements are unchanged (checked: `git diff origin/main --stat -- infra/gerrit` is empty).\n- [ ] The `AGENTS.md` \"land it yourself\" instruction needs no edit, because `scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py` already lands with the `RebarBotNava` credential (checked: `git diff origin/main --stat -- AGENTS.md` is empty).\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A merged change records `RebarBotNava`, not the administrator, as submitter, with votes cast by the two bots.\n      provenance: environment=production Gerrit rebar.solutions.navateam.com; principal=RebarBotNava via git credential fill; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call - changes 3109 and 3110 queried 2026-10-25 show owner and submitter RebarBotNava, LLM-Review by rebar-review-bot, Verified by rebar-ci-bot; recorded as a ticket comment.\n- [ ] The change depends on no single CI provider (checked: documentation wording only).\n- [ ] `make verify` shows no failure outside the known pandoc set, and the Gerrit change is `Verified +1`.\n\n## Out of scope\nSplitting the `Verified` and `LLM-Review` vote permissions between the two service accounts, and making `scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py` work in a sandbox that cannot run `git credential fill` (its own defect).\n"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792957208131443001,"uuid":"87a4ec10-b5a6-40b6-ac83-028d6c82934a"}